<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sinmun of Silla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 692</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sinmun was king of Silla from 681 to 692, son of King Munmu. He put down a rebellion of nobles early in his reign and built the institutions of Unified Silla, dividing the realm into nine provinces and five secondary capitals and founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gukhak">Gukhak</a>, the national Confucian academy, in 682. In 689 he replaced the officials' stipend villages with salaries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sinmun-of-silla.jpg" alt="Sinmun of Silla" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ronnie Dayo · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%EC%8B%A0%EB%AC%B8%EC%99%95%EB%A6%89_Historical_site_no._181.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
